From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:26:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] arm64: dts: apple: t602x: Add the tunneled PCIe
 controllers

Describe the PCIe controller and IOMMU behind each of the four USB4
host routers of a die, from the Apple device tree of a Mac Studio (M2
Ultra): registers, interrupts, MSI ranges and windows of apciec0-5 and
dart-apciec0-5, power domain ATCn_PCIE. The ACIO nodes gain the adapter
registers and a link to the root port of their controller.

The nodes are disabled by default. Enable the six that have a port on
the Mac Studio (j475d), and add the aliases through which m1n1 fills in
the tunables (usb4_N_pcie, usb4_N_pcie_adapter).

All devices behind a tunnel share one IOMMU stream, which keeps the map
to one line. The 64-bit window is not translated, so its bus address
carries the die offset. The controllers get fixed PCI domains 8-15:
they probe without waiting for a reset pin, and would otherwise take
domain 0 from the internal controller whenever that one defers.

Check: all 110 Apple device trees build; the decompiled j475d tree has
the six controllers, domains 8-13, die 1 at bus address 0x28_00000000.
